.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Security policy: the only key exchange methods, host key and signature algorithms, ciphers and compression methods foxtrot will ever negotiate.
.PP
The lists here are closed.  Anything absent (SSH\-1, CBC and CTR ciphers, RC4, 3DES, Blowfish, separate MACs of any kind, hmac\-sha1, finite\-field Diffie\-Hellman groups and group exchange, SHA\-1 anywhere, ssh\-rsa (as an algorithm; the name remains as a key type), ssh\-dss, ECDSA over P\-521, zlib compression, the "none" cipher, "none" authentication of the host) is not a configuration option; it is not implemented.  The "Security policy" chapter of the manual gives the reasoning behind each choice.
.PP
Algorithm names are the IANA SSH registry names (RFC 4250 section 4.6 and the later RFCs and drafts that registered them).
.SH "TYPES AND CONSTANTS"
.PP
.nf
#define GF_PROTOCOL_VERSION "2.0"
.fi
.RS
The only protocol version: RFC 4253 section 4.2 "SSH\-2.0\-...".
.RE
.PP
.nf
enum gf_kex
{
  GF_KEX_CURVE25519_SHA256 = 1,		/* RFC 8731 */
  GF_KEX_MLKEM768X25519_SHA256,		/* draft\-ietf\-sshm\-mlkem\-hybrid\-kex */
  GF_KEX_MLKEM768NISTP256_SHA256,	/* same draft */
  GF_KEX_MLKEM1024NISTP384_SHA384,	/* same draft */
  GF_KEX_SNTRUP761X25519_SHA512,	/* draft\-ietf\-sshm\-ntruprime\-ssh;
					   also the OpenSSH 9.0 name with
					   "@openssh.com" appended */
  GF_KEX_ECDH_NISTP256_SHA256,		/* RFC 5656 */
  GF_KEX_ECDH_NISTP384_SHA384		/* RFC 5656 */
};
.fi
.RS
Key exchange methods.  Every one is an ephemeral key agreement in the style of RFC 5656 (ECDH_INIT and ECDH_REPLY, or their hybrid names KEX_HYBRID_INIT and KEX_HYBRID_REPLY), signed by the server's host key.
.RE
.PP
.nf
enum gf_sigalg
{
  GF_SIG_ED25519 = 1,		/* ssh\-ed25519, RFC 8709 */
  GF_SIG_ECDSA_NISTP256,	/* ecdsa\-sha2\-nistp256, RFC 5656 */
  GF_SIG_ECDSA_NISTP384,	/* ecdsa\-sha2\-nistp384, RFC 5656 */
  GF_SIG_RSA_SHA2_256,		/* rsa\-sha2\-256, RFC 8332 */
  GF_SIG_RSA_SHA2_512,		/* rsa\-sha2\-512, RFC 8332 */
  GF_SIG_ED25519_CERT,		/* ssh\-ed25519\-cert\-v01@openssh.com */
  GF_SIG_ECDSA_NISTP256_CERT,	/* ecdsa\-sha2\-nistp256\-cert\-v01@openssh.com */
  GF_SIG_ECDSA_NISTP384_CERT,	/* ecdsa\-sha2\-nistp384\-cert\-v01@openssh.com */
  GF_SIG_RSA_SHA2_256_CERT,	/* rsa\-sha2\-256\-cert\-v01@openssh.com */
  GF_SIG_RSA_SHA2_512_CERT,	/* rsa\-sha2\-512\-cert\-v01@openssh.com */
  /* FIDO security keys (OpenSSH PROTOCOL.u2f), which sign on a token and
     are for user authentication only: never a host key.  */
  GF_SIG_SK_ED25519,		/* sk\-ssh\-ed25519@openssh.com */
  GF_SIG_SK_ECDSA_NISTP256,	/* sk\-ecdsa\-sha2\-nistp256@openssh.com */
  GF_SIG_SK_ED25519_CERT,	/* sk\-ssh\-ed25519\-cert\-v01@openssh.com */
  GF_SIG_SK_ECDSA_NISTP256_CERT,	/* sk\-ecdsa\-sha2\-nistp256\-cert\-v01@openssh.com */
  /* X.509 certificate chains as keys (RFC 6187), with the signatures of the
     key in the end certificate.  x509v3\-ssh\-rsa (SHA\-1), x509v3\-ssh\-dss and
     the P\-521 curve are not here.  */
  GF_SIG_X509_ECDSA_NISTP256,	/* x509v3\-ecdsa\-sha2\-nistp256 */
  GF_SIG_X509_ECDSA_NISTP384,	/* x509v3\-ecdsa\-sha2\-nistp384 */
  GF_SIG_X509_RSA2048_SHA256	/* x509v3\-rsa2048\-sha256 */
};
.fi
.RS
Signature algorithms for host keys and for public key authentication. Each names a key type and a signature format at once, as SSH does.  The certificate algorithms (OpenSSH PROTOCOL.certkeys) present a certificate as the key and sign with the key inside it, in the format of the plain algorithm: the signature of "ssh\-ed25519\-cert\-v01@openssh.com" is an "ssh\-ed25519" signature.
.RE
.PP
.nf
enum gf_cipher
{
  GF_CIPHER_NONE = 0,		/* Before the first key exchange only.  */
  GF_CIPHER_CHACHA20_POLY1305 = 1,	/* chacha20\-poly1305@openssh.com */
  GF_CIPHER_AES256_GCM,		/* aes256\-gcm@openssh.com, RFC 5647 */
  GF_CIPHER_AES128_GCM		/* aes128\-gcm@openssh.com, RFC 5647 */
};
.fi
.RS
Ciphers.  AEAD only: the packet is authenticated by the cipher itself, so the MAC lists of KEXINIT are empty and ignored.
.RE
.PP
.nf
#define GF_MIN_RSA_BITS 2048
.fi
.RS
The smallest RSA modulus accepted in a host key or a user key (112\-bit security, the floor quickstep's trust layer also uses).
.RE
.PP
.nf
#define GF_KEX_STRICT_CLIENT "kex\-strict\-c\-v00@openssh.com"
.fi
.RS
Strict key exchange markers (OpenSSH PROTOCOL, "Terrapin" fix).  The client adds the first to its key exchange list and the server the second; each side requires the other's.
.RE
.PP
.nf
#define GF_KEX_STRICT_SERVER "kex\-strict\-s\-v00@openssh.com"
.fi
.PP
.nf
#define GF_KEX_EXTINFO_CLIENT "ext\-info\-c"
.fi
.RS
Extension negotiation (RFC 8308).
.RE
.PP
.nf
#define GF_KEX_EXTINFO_SERVER "ext\-info\-s"
.fi
