Names.  The *_name functions return the preferred name of an algorithm, or NULL for an unknown value.  The *_from_name functions take a name of N bytes (not NUL\-terminated) and return the algorithm, or 0 for anything the policy does not permit, including every name that appears nowhere in this file.
.TP
const enum gf_kex *\fBgf_policy_default_kex\fP (size_t *n);
Default preference\-ordered lists.  Each returns a static array and stores its length in *N.  An application may pass a list of its own to a connection (any subset, any order), but only of these.
.TP
const enum gf_sigalg *\fBgf_policy_default_sigalgs\fP (size_t *n);
.br
const enum gf_sigalg *\fBgf_policy_user_sigalgs\fP (size_t *n);
.br
const enum gf_cipher *\fBgf_policy_default_ciphers\fP (size_t *n);
The sigalgs list is for host keys: it has no security\-key algorithm, which a host cannot have.  The user list is what a server takes from users and announces in server\-sig\-algs: plain names only, a certificate being signed for with the algorithm of its key.
.PP
Key exchange properties.
.TP
